WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.082 --> 00:00:03.652
- The compliments from people,
kind of praising me for

00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:05.881
losing weight that I didn't need to lose,

00:00:05.881 --> 00:00:06.941
it really did, like,

00:00:06.941 --> 00:00:09.797
help kick start a full on eating disorder.

00:00:12.947 --> 00:00:14.666
- You know, your aunts or uncles,

00:00:14.666 --> 00:00:15.787
or your parents, whatever,

00:00:15.787 --> 00:00:18.348
might say something to
you thinking that it's

00:00:18.348 --> 00:00:19.647
just an observation.

00:00:19.647 --> 00:00:22.027
- I know that people
mean well when they say,

00:00:22.027 --> 00:00:23.437
especially like, you look good,

00:00:23.437 --> 00:00:24.326
have you lost weight?

00:00:24.326 --> 00:00:25.332
- You would think that, like,

00:00:25.332 --> 00:00:26.845
getting compliments about your weight,

00:00:26.845 --> 00:00:28.740
and how you look is always gonna be, like,

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.180
a positive thing, if it's
like, a positive comment.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.720
- When I was 15 years old,

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.960
I was put on this medication,

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.680
and a side effect was weight loss,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:37.979
and this girl came up to me,

00:00:37.979 --> 00:00:39.500
she's like, "Oh my God, Mandy,

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:40.940
"I want your hip bones."

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.960
Over, like, a year and a half,

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.516
I lost, like, 20 more pounds.

00:00:45.516 --> 00:00:48.436
The compliments kind of
stopped at some point,

00:00:48.436 --> 00:00:51.596
because it really became
obvious that it wasn't

00:00:51.596 --> 00:00:52.876
good anymore.

00:00:52.876 --> 00:00:55.375
- In college, I went through
a really tough time where I

00:00:55.375 --> 00:00:57.396
was starving myself essentially.

00:00:57.396 --> 00:00:59.776
People were reinforcing
it by saying, like,

00:00:59.776 --> 00:01:01.236
"Oh, you look like, so great!"

00:01:01.236 --> 00:01:03.036
like, "you look so fit."

00:01:03.036 --> 00:01:05.597
I was not fit, I was not fit mentally,

00:01:05.597 --> 00:01:07.256
and I was not fit physically.

00:01:07.256 --> 00:01:08.455
- I lost a lot of weight,

00:01:08.455 --> 00:01:11.116
like I went from maybe, like a 12, 10,

00:01:11.116 --> 00:01:13.676
to a 6, 4, and I came
back after the summer,

00:01:13.676 --> 00:01:16.978
before I even said hello to
people, everyone was like,

00:01:16.978 --> 00:01:19.058
"Oh my God! You look so great!

00:01:19.058 --> 00:01:20.198
"You look amazing!"

00:01:20.198 --> 00:01:22.740
I didn't really know how to
feel because I didn't lose the

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.160
weight on purpose,

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.070
and I didn't lose it in a healthy way,

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.823
like, I was just really sad
and depressed that whole

00:01:28.823 --> 00:01:29.654
school year.

00:01:29.654 --> 00:01:32.344
- I lost a ton of weight
after a really bad breakup,

00:01:32.344 --> 00:01:35.524
and I remember going
out for the first time,

00:01:35.524 --> 00:01:38.495
in like a month, and my
friends looking at me,

00:01:38.495 --> 00:01:40.283
and being like, "Oh, you look so good!

00:01:40.283 --> 00:01:41.840
"You lost so much weight!"

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.440
I had, like, conflicted feelings.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.280
I was, like, yeah, I'm thin,

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:46.760
and now I can, like, go out,

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:47.750
and get a better guy,

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:48.919
but at the same time, I was, like,

00:01:48.919 --> 00:01:51.100
well, I'm thin because I've
been lying on my bed for

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.160
the past month and a half.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.279
- After I gave birth, people
were already mentioning that,

00:01:55.279 --> 00:01:56.380
"Hey, you look great!"

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.900
And, hey, "you're already
losing the baby weight."

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.300
A lot of women are posting
their progress throughout

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:04.881
the pregnancy, and then their
progress post-pregnancy,

00:02:04.881 --> 00:02:07.500
so there's a lot of
pressure to be able to keep

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.439
up with that.

00:02:08.439 --> 00:02:10.060
- I, like, created this pressure,

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.980
and this fear of, what
happens if I don't keep it up,

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.161
if I don't maintain it.

00:02:14.161 --> 00:02:17.060
- I think in general, we have
to take a little bit more

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:19.480
of an emphasis away from the number.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:20.940
- Complimenting somebody's weight,

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.980
I don't think is the best
compliment you can give, period.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.600
- I feel like, not all
weight loss is intentional.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:26.681
- Just tell them, like,

00:02:26.681 --> 00:02:27.941
hey, you're looking great today,

00:02:27.941 --> 00:02:29.150
even if it's just saying, like,

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:29.931
hey, cool shirt.

00:02:29.931 --> 00:02:31.292
You don't need to make it about weight.

00:02:31.292 --> 00:02:32.552
- I like that when people said,

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.732
oh, like, your chest is out,

00:02:34.732 --> 00:02:36.052
like, I don't know,

00:02:36.052 --> 00:02:39.472
like, something that, noticed
my new found confidence.

00:02:39.472 --> 00:02:42.772
- If I'm happy with
myself, then it's all good.

00:02:42.772 --> 00:02:44.642
(upbeat music)

